Chaikin Money Flow measures the amount of money flowing into or out of an asset by comparing the closing price to the high-low range, weighted by volume. It complements NATR by providing insights into the *quality* and *conviction* of price movements, indicating whether buying or selling pressure is accumulating over time. A strong positive CMF suggests robust accumulation supporting upward breakouts, while a strong negative CMF indicates strong distribution favoring downward breakouts, enhancing the reliability of the strategy's volume-filtered entries.
