Indicator Name: Absolute Money Flow Index Deviation (AMFID)

This indicator gauges the strength of money flowing into or out of an asset by combining price and volume. While NATR filters for sufficient overall volatility, AMFID complements it by focusing on **Volume Efficiency** and **Momentum Stability**. A high AMFID value indicates strong directional conviction (either strong buying or strong selling pressure) supported by significant volume. This environment makes breakouts more likely to be genuine and sustained, increasing the probability of the strategy's success by filtering for assets with clear and volume-confirmed market pressure.
