The KAMA Efficiency Ratio measures the linearity of price movement, ranging from 0 (noisy, non-trending) to 1 (smooth, directional trend). A high ER complements NATR by distinguishing between volatile, but choppy, markets and volatile markets that are exhibiting strong, efficient trends, providing a robust environment for channel breakouts.
