Indicator Name: **Vortex Indicator (Absolute Difference)**

The Vortex Indicator measures the strength and direction of a trend, providing insights into directional movement. By taking the absolute difference between the positive (+VI) and negative (-VI) components, this indicator quantifies the overall clarity and persistence of the trend. It complements NATR by filtering for assets that not only exhibit sufficient volatility but also show clear, sustained directional movement, thereby identifying cleaner trend environments where channel breakouts are more likely to be robust and less prone to whipsaws.
