Indicator Name: Trend Acceleration Index (TAI)
This indicator measures the absolute rate of change of the spread between the fast and slow Simple Moving Averages, smoothed to provide a stable measure of trend acceleration. A high TAI value indicates a strong, accelerating trend (either up or down) where momentum breakouts are more likely to be sustained, complementing NATR by focusing on trend quality and momentum stability rather than just volatility.
