Indicator Name: MFI Conviction Score

This indicator measures the strength and conviction of money flow supporting price movements. By taking the absolute deviation of the Money Flow Index (MFI) from 50, it assigns a higher score to assets exhibiting strong buying or selling pressure, regardless of direction. This complements NATR by filtering for assets where volatility is coupled with clear, sustained capital flow, making channel breakouts more reliable when confirmed by trend and volume.
