Indicator Name: Normalized Smoothed Trend Momentum (NSTM)
The Normalized Smoothed Trend Momentum (NSTM) quantifies the vigor and consistency of the underlying trend by measuring the percentage change of a fast Simple Moving Average (SMA) over a defined period. This indicator complements NATR, which ensures sufficient volatility, by filtering for assets exhibiting strong, stable, and directional price movement, making them more conducive for successful channel breakouts.
