Indicator Name: Trend Persistence Score (TPS)
This indicator measures the consistency and strength of the trend by applying the Relative Strength Index (RSI) to the difference between the fast and slow Simple Moving Averages. A high absolute deviation from 50 in this "RSI of SMA Difference" suggests that the gap between the SMAs is consistently widening or narrowing, indicating a robust and persistent trend suitable for channel breakouts. It complements NATR by focusing on the quality and stability of the underlying trend rather than just raw volatility.
