Indicator Name: Volume-Weighted Momentum Strength (VWMS)
This indicator measures the strength and stability of price momentum, explicitly confirming it with consistent trading volume. It calculates the Rate of Change (momentum) and weights it by a Volume Efficiency Ratio (current volume relative to average volume), then smooths the result and takes its absolute value. This approach identifies environments where price movements are not only significant but are also robustly supported by strong volume, complementing NATR's volatility assessment by focusing on the *quality* of directional movement and volume conviction for the strategy's channel breakouts.
