Indicator Name: Trend-Aligned Directional Strength (TADS)
This indicator quantifies the strength of directional conviction that aligns with the strategy's existing SMA-based trend filter. By measuring the difference between positive and negative directional movement indices (DMI) and then only scoring when this directional bias confirms the SMA trend, TADS highlights assets exhibiting robust and confirmed trends. It complements NATR by focusing on the quality and stability of the trend's direction and momentum, crucial for successful breakout continuation, rather than merely asset volatility.
