--------------------
Indicator Name: Absolute Normalized Moving Average Slope (ANMAS)
This indicator measures the steepness of the long-term trend, normalized by the asset's recent volatility. A high ANMAS score indicates a strong, well-defined trend (either up or down) where the underlying moving average is consistently moving in one direction relative to the typical price fluctuation. This complements NATR (which ensures general volatility) by focusing on the *directional consistency* of that volatility. For a channel breakout strategy with an SMA trend filter, a robust and persistent underlying trend, as quantified by a high ANMAS, provides a more reliable environment for breakouts to succeed and continue their momentum.
