Indicator Name: Smoothed Efficiency Ratio (SER)
This indicator quantifies the "directness" or "efficiency" of price movement over a defined period, smoothed to provide a more stable trend quality score. A high SER indicates that price is moving in a relatively straight line, demonstrating strong, sustained momentum with minimal choppiness. This complements NATR by filtering for assets where the existing volatility is channeled into clear, reliable trends, which is crucial for a channel breakout strategy to succeed and avoid false signals.
