Indicator Name: Absolute MACD Histogram

The Absolute MACD Histogram serves as an excellent measure of **Momentum Stability and Trend Quality** by quantifying the acceleration or deceleration of momentum within an existing trend. A high absolute MACD Histogram value signifies a strong, accelerating trend (either bullish or bearish), indicating high conviction in the price movement. This provides a robust "quality filter" for the Volume-Filtered Channel Momentum strategy, complementing NATR by selecting assets where price movements are backed by powerful, consistent momentum, thereby increasing the probability of successful breakouts and follow-through.
