Indicator Name: Smoothed Absolute Detrended Price Oscillator (SADPO)
SADPO measures the magnitude of price deviation from a cycle-filtered moving average, providing a score for how strongly and consistently price is moving away from its short-term equilibrium. A high SADPO indicates a committed trend, making breakout signals more reliable. It complements NATR by focusing on the 'quality' of directional movement rather than just raw volatility.
