Indicator Name: Smoothed Trend Line Fit (STLF)
The Smoothed Trend Line Fit (STLF) measures the linearity and consistency of price movement within a specified lookback period using the R-squared value of a linear regression, then smooths this measure. A high STLF value indicates a clear, well-defined trend, providing an ideal environment for the channel breakout strategy to identify sustained momentum rather than whipsaws, effectively complementing NATR by focusing on trend quality over mere volatility.
