Indicator Name: Absolute MACD Trend Strength (AMTS)
This indicator measures the absolute divergence between a fast and slow Exponential Moving Average (the MACD line). A higher absolute value signifies a clearer and more forceful trend, irrespective of its direction (up or down). While NATR ensures sufficient volatility in assets, AMTS ensures this volatility is channeled into a persistent, strong directional movement, providing a robust environment for the strategy's channel breakout and trend-following components to succeed.
