Indicator Name: Volume Price Flow (VPF)
Volume Price Flow (VPF) quantifies the smoothed average directional volume pressure per candle, derived from how much of each candle's volume occurs closer to its high or low. Complementing NATR's volatility assessment, VPF provides insight into the underlying buying or selling conviction (volume efficiency) driving price movements. A high absolute VPF value indicates strong, consistent directional pressure, suggesting better trend quality and a higher probability of successful, sustained channel breakouts.
