Indicator Name: Volume-Weighted Trend Confidence (VWTC) Score
This indicator measures the stability and conviction of a trend by combining the asset's price deviation from its Volume-Weighted Average Price (VWAP) with the momentum of the VWAP itself. A high score indicates that price is confidently positioned relative to a strongly trending VWAP (e.g., price well above a rising VWAP or well below a falling VWAP), signaling a robust, volume-backed trend suitable for breakouts, thus complementing NATR by focusing on trend quality rather than just volatility.
