Indicator Name: Guppy Trend Stability Score (GTSS)

The Guppy Trend Stability Score (GTSS) complements NATR by evaluating the *quality and stability* of a trend, rather than just its volatility magnitude. While NATR confirms sufficient price movement, GTSS quantifies how orderly and persistent that movement is by measuring the separation between groups of fast and slow Simple Moving Averages. A high GTSS indicates a robust, well-established trend where short-term speculative movements are aligned with longer-term investor trends, creating an environment where channel breakouts are more likely to find sustained follow-through, increasing the probability of the strategy's success.
