Indicator Name: Normalized Price Trend Displace (NPTD)

This indicator measures the magnitude of an asset's price displacement from its longer-term average, normalized by its recent local volatility. A high NPTD score signifies a strong, sustained trend where the price has moved significantly away from its long-term equilibrium relative to its typical short-term fluctuations. This identifies assets with robust directional conviction, which are ideal environments for the channel momentum strategy to capture high-probability breakouts with follow-through. It complements NATR by focusing on the *quality and persistence* of the trend rather than just its absolute volatility.
