Indicator Name: Absolute Normalized VWAP Slope

This indicator measures the strength and consistency of the underlying trend by quantifying the normalized slope of the Volume-Weighted Average Price (VWAP). A high absolute slope indicates a strong, sustained, and volume-confirmed directional movement. This complements NATR (which ensures sufficient volatility) by identifying assets where price movement exhibits strong conviction and efficiency, making them more likely to experience clean channel breakouts that align with a robust prevailing trend, thus increasing the probability of the strategy's success.
